metag: unwind through signal frames

libgcc had no MD_FALLBACK_FRAME_STATE_FOR for Meta Linux.  An unwinder that
reaches a signal handler's return address -- the sigreturn trampoline at the
end of the kernel's rt_sigframe -- found no FDE and stopped, so a thread
cancelled in a blocking system call never ran its cleanup handlers and C++
destructors: uClibc-ng's tst-cancelx4/16/18/20/21, tst-cleanupx1/3 and
tst-oncex3/4 with -fexceptions.

Recognise the trampoline (MOV D1Re0, #__NR_rt_sigreturn; SWITCH #0x440001)
and restore the registers that have an unwind column from the sigcontext.
The Meta port keeps only 13 columns (DWARF_REG_TO_UNWIND_COLUMN): the
callee-saved registers, D1RtP, A0StP, A0FrP and A1LbP.  The interrupted PC
needs one of its own -- D1RtP, the return column, holds a live value there,
the same arrangement as on csky and microblaze -- so the PC (register 54)
gets a fourteenth.

